WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.767
-Thank you and welcome, welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:04.367
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.067
You're here!

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:07.701
Thank you for watching!

00:00:07.701 --> 00:00:09.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:11.334
Well, this is amazing.

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:13.434
Here in New York City, we're just a few days away

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.601
from breaking the record for the longest stretch

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:17.634
of winter without snow.

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:20.334
[ Audience cheers ] It's weird.

00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:22.734
It's like Mother Nature is doing dry January.

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:24.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.634
I miss the snow.

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:27.234
It's just not the same taking your kids sledding

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:29.734
down a pile of trash bags. You know, it's just not...

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:31.367
Let's get to some news here.

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:33.567
Everyone's still talking about all the classified documents

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:36.501
that keep popping up, and now spokespeople are saying

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.100
that until the end of their terms,

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.267
all classified documents were returned

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:43.334
by Obama, Bush, and Clinton.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:45.567
In other words, we're five minutes away from learning

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:46.968
that they found documents

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:49.834
at the homes of Obama, Bush, and Clinton.

00:00:49.834 --> 00:00:52.000
Meanwhile, when asked if he had any classified documents,

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.200
Dick Cheney put his heart into sleep mode.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.367 --> 00:00:59.534
[ Applause ]

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.067
That's right. All the presidents said

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:08.534
they don't have any classified documents.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.167
Then Jimmy Carter was like, "Uh, hello.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:12.234
I'm still here, too. Hi."

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:13.534
Actually, just to be safe,

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.934
the FBI is searching Jimmy Carter's dollhouse.

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:18.634
[ Audience awws ]

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:21.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:23.434
It's the oddest photo I've ever seen.

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:25.634
-The weirdest. -It's the weirdest photo ever.

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:28.100
It seems like there's so much going on right now.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.267
Donald Trump, Joe Biden, now Mike Pence --

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:32.534
all have classified documents in their homes.

00:01:32.534 --> 00:01:35.100
The NFL playoffs are in full swing.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.601
The NFL this weekend.

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:39.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.868
Egg prices are soaring.

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:45.033
And Dunkin' is making plans

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:47.133
to offer their own alcoholic beverages.

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.167
[ Audience cheers ] There's a lot to go over.

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:50.834
Let's just jump in, cover it all at once.

00:01:50.834 --> 00:01:52.534
It's time for a "News Smash." Here we go.

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:57.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:59.634
First up, the classified documents scandal.

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:02.567
They just keep finding more. First it was Trump, then Biden.

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:05.634
Now Mike Pence. At this point, Americans are tired of it.

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.534
They just want to turn off the news and watch...

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:09.534
the NFL playoffs.

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:10.934
This weekend.

00:02:10.934 --> 00:02:14.400
It's Bengals versus Chiefs, 49ers versus Eagles...

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:17.901
...for a trip to the Super Bowl.

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:20.400
The stakes are high. Almost as high as...

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.000
egg prices.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.567
They are soaring,

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:26.067
and Congress might even investigate what's going on.

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:28.367
At these prices, instead of eating eggs for breakfast,

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:32.133
you're better off... drinking booze at Dunkin'.

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:33.767
That's right. Dunkin' is planning

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:36.033
to sell its own alcoholic drinks.

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.868
People were like, "Ew, what's even in it?"

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:39.834
And Dunkin' said... "That's classified."

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:42.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.734
[ Applause ]

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:49.234
The papers -- The papers are everywhere.

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:50.968
This week, President Biden was like,

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:53.534
"I apologize for keeping documents in ma-garage,

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:54.868
ma-office, and...

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:56.200
ma-homes."

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.801
That is the Kansas City quarterback.

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:00.801
And he's got to play Cincinnati's Joe Burrow.

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:02.234
Both of them are going to play hard.

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:04.567
Neither one is gonna just roll over easy...

00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:06.167
scrambled, fried.

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:08.234
No matter how you make them, they're expensive.

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:10.501
So if you've got a bunch of eggs right now, keep them to yourself.

00:03:10.501 --> 00:03:11.634
Maybe even...

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:12.801
hide them.

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:16.367
Mike Pence -- Mike Pence has been so stressed,

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:18.200
he's thinking about doing shots over at...

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.734
Drunkin' Donuts.

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:22.100
Seriously, booze at Dunkin'?

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.334
Even people in Boston are like, "Sorry, but I think I'll...

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:26.467
pass." That's the quarterback's job.

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:29.100
And if they screw up on Sunday, their whole season will be...

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.601
totally wasted.

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:34.300
In conclusion, don't miss, kickers...

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.868
stop it, misters...

00:03:35.868 --> 00:03:37.734
penny pinch-ahs...

00:03:37.734 --> 00:03:39.267
wicked piss-ah.

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:40.934
This has been a "News Smash."

00:03:40.934 --> 00:03:43.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:47.067
♪♪

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:48.834
Well, guys, get this.

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:50.968
I read that King Charles'

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:53.334
real-estate firm is suing Twitter

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:56.534
for failing to pay rent at their London office.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:59.133
Yeah, King Charles' real-estate firm.

00:03:59.133 --> 00:04:02.634
Everyone's like, "You mean...England?"

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:05.167
You know your landlord is the king when your eviction notice

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:08.434
starts with the phrase, "Hear ye, hear ye."

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:10.501
Hey, I heard that due to some major delays,

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:13.067
Paris is rushing to finish construction work

00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:15.734
in time for the 2024 Olympics.

00:04:15.734 --> 00:04:17.701
Yeah, the French workers were like -- [Inhales sharply]

00:04:17.701 --> 00:04:20.501
[French accent] "We are working 24/7.

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:23.234
That's 24 hours a month. 7 months a year."

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:27.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:31.133
Apparently, the delays have been caused by a steel shortage.

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:33.234
Yeah, you know it's rough when they have to strip

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:35.701
the Eiffel Tower for parts.

00:04:35.701 --> 00:04:37.434
Switching gears, did you guys see this?

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:40.033
Justin Bieber just sold his entire music catalog

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:42.434
for $200 million.

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:44.634
Yeah, asked what he's going to do with the money, Bieber said,

00:04:44.634 --> 00:04:47.234
"Buy a dozen eggs."

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:50.033
$200 million -- that's one dollar for every person

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:52.400
who pretended to know all the words to "Despacito."

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.300
[ Laughter ] Well, this is wild.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:57.601
The city of Philadelphia is so desperate for lifeguards

00:04:57.601 --> 00:05:00.934
that they're recruiting applicants who can't swim.

00:05:00.934 --> 00:05:04.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:06.868
Even worse, they're letting the lifeguards work from home.

00:05:06.868 --> 00:05:08.133
You don't see how that would...

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:10.167
-What, do they Zoom in? -[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:05:10.167 --> 00:05:13.167
And finally, two men in Germany just broke the world record

00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:15.968
by playing the accordion for 24 hours straight.

00:05:15.968 --> 00:05:17.667
I don't know what's harder --

00:05:17.667 --> 00:05:19.801
playing the accordion for 24 hours

00:05:19.801 --> 00:05:22.167
or listening to the accordion for 24 hours.

00:05:22.167 --> 00:05:23.801
We have a great show tonight.

